    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7632" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cestus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caest-</span></b> ) or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ŏs</span></b> , i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεστός</span> (lit. stitched, embroidered; hence,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>subst.;</i> cf.
			Lidd. and Scott under <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεστός</span>), <i>a girdle</i>, <i>tie</i>, <i>belt</i>, <i>girth</i>, <i>strap</i>, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
			25</span></i> Schneid. <i>N. cr.;</i>
			<i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 8,
			6</span></i>.—Particularly, <i>the girdle of
				Venus</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 6, 138</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 206</span></i> sq.;
					<i><span class="en">Serv. ad Verg. A. 5,
		69</span></i>.</div>
